	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE: ENEPAQ TEMPERATURE SENSORS\n\n1. Each Enepaq 1x4 module has one 2-wire sensor output (hottest of its sensors, analog OR'd). The sensor is a shunt voltage reference (\"zener-like\"), NOT an NTC: Vout is set by temperature, not by bias current.\n2. Vout vs temp (Enepaq Table 4): -40°C 2.44 V | 25°C 1.86 V | 60°C 1.51 V | 120°C 1.30 V. Use linear interpolation.\n3. Bias: TBIAS (≈4.7 V) through 3.3 kΩ gives 0.7-1.0 mA per sensor(spec 0.4-15 mA). 8 sensors ≈ 8 mA from TSREF (limit ≥15 mA).\n4. Read the absolute GPIO voltage and convert with Table 4. Do not use TI's NTC ratiometric formula. D2's drop only changes bias current, not the reading.\n5. Sensor is isolated from the cells up to 60 V. Fine at 8S (33.6 V max); re-check if module count per slave grows.\n6. R31-R38 / C29-C36: 10 kΩ / 0.1 µF filter (fc ≈ 160 Hz). The 10 kΩ also limits GPIO clamp current on a harness fault."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 132.08 0)
		(size 68.58 38.1)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2dda1d08-c8d6-4dfa-b259-121b5536ebaa")
	)
	(text_box "D2: blocks back-feed into TSREF if a TMP wire shorts to a cell tap. ~0.3 V drop is harmless withshunt-reference sensors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 45.72 76.2 0)
		(size 40.64 10.2572)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a8728048-e500-492d-ae7b-04745b64a194")
	)
	(text_box "LAYOUT NOTE: TEMPERATURE SENSE\n\n1. Place R23-R38 and C29-C36 at J3. Filter caps return to GND beside J3 pins 19/20 so harness noise goes straight back out the connector, not under U1.\n2. Sensor returns share J3-19/20 with U1's supply return. Never join them to TAP0 (J3-17) on either board.\n3. Filtered GPIO1-8 traces may run the length of the board; keep them over the GND plane, away from COMH/COML.\n4. Add 2-3 GND vias at J3-19/20.\n5. TBIAS trace carries ≈8 mA DC; 0.2 mm min width."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 99.06 0)
		(size 68.58 27.826)
		(margins 2.25 2.25 2.25 2.25)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 255 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 0 255 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ad62bbce-fdcb-4586-93fb-96048130539a")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE: BQ7961x COMPARATOR SETTINGS (SLUSE81F 7.3.x)\n\n1. OT comparator (10-39 % of TSREF) works with these sensors:\nOT_THR 31 % = 1.55 V ≈ 55°C (margin under 60°C); 30 % ≈ 61°C.\nHysteresis 2 % ≈ 0.1 V.\n2. UT comparator (66-80 %) cannot detect cold (sensor max 2.44 V = 49 %). Use it as an OPEN-WIRE detector: an open sensor pulls GPIO to TBIAS (≈94 %) and trips UT. A shorted sensor trips OT.\n3. OTCB (10-24 % = 0.5-1.2 V) can never trigger (sensor floor 1.30 V). Balancing thermal limits are firmware + die temp only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 45.72 93.98 0)
		(size 83.82 27.94)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 250 236 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b5564efe-2855-4f28-9c3d-9af9b811369b")
	)
